// Title: Sensitive File Dump Via Wbadmin.EXE
// ID: 8b93a509-1cb8-42e1-97aa-ee24224cdc15
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems), frack113
// Date: 2024-05-10
// Tags: attack.credential-access, attack.t1003.003
// Description: Detects the dump of highly sensitive files such as "NTDS.DIT" and "SECURITY" hive.
// Attackers can leverage the "wbadmin" utility in order to dump sensitive files that might contain credential or sensitive information.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

process where (((process.command_line like "*_start*" or process.command_line like "*_backup*")) and ((process.executable endswith "\\wbadmin.exe") or (process.pe.original_file_name == "WBADMIN.EXE")) and ((process.command_line like "*_\\config\\SAM*" or process.command_line like "*_\\config\\SECURITY*" or process.command_line like "*_\\config\\SYSTEM*" or process.command_line like "*_\\Windows\\NTDS\\NTDS.dit*")))
